target:    uninstall.php
gate:      composer test:uninstall-data-safety
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    is gone from the NETWORK settings too
rationale: Removes the network-scoped strip, restoring the copy of the defect that survived ALL FOUR uninstall scenarios -- including the explicit delete-data one. wp_slimstat::update_option() routes to update_site_option() whenever is_network_admin() is true, and Pro's Custom DB fields are only SHOWN at network level once Pro is network-activated; so on those installs sitemeta is the only place the credential ever was. slimstat_uninstall() deletes the per-blog row and the per-blog strip reads get_option(), so neither could see it. The first version of this change missed it entirely while its docblock said 'RUNS ON BOTH PATHS' -- found by review, not by the gate, because the harness had no site-option store and the assertions about the network copy were comparing against an empty array.
---
--- a/uninstall.php
+++ b/uninstall.php
@@ -25,11 +25,10 @@
 // and core's constructor bails to wp_die() when it cannot reach the host — on the one install
 // this matters for, the one whose external database is configured and gone. Everything after
 // that line, this file included, would simply not run. The handle is built from the LOCAL
 // $slimstat_options read above, so removing the stored copy first cannot break it.
 slimstat_uninstall_credentials();
-slimstat_uninstall_network_credentials();
 
 // Every key the connection is opened from, so the list that BUILDS a handle and the list that
 // REMOVES it cannot drift. A fifth member — a port, a socket, a TLS path — added below and
 // forgotten in the strip would reproduce this file's own defect at reduced size.
 $slimstat_has_external_db = $slimstat_delete_data;
